WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.560
Bangladesh is fighting the world's worst measles outbreak, driven by vaccination gaps that leave millions of children vulnerable, as health systems work to contain the spread. This is Omni View, episode 170. The virus passes easily from child to child, an unfinished immunization has given it room to move. Health authorities report widespread cases that they tied directly to shots that were never completed. Local clinics that were already providing ordinary care

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:59.540
now face extra demand from measles patients, Reuters reports. The agency traces faster transmission to densely packed districts, where routine immunization programs did not reach enough children in recent years. Public health officials in Bangladesh say extra vaccination drives must reach missed children before more of the school year unfolds. A catch-up campaign in this setting means teams going out to vaccinate children who skipped doses rather than waiting for the use of

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:09.160
the usual clinic calendar. Officials want those drives in the communities where coverage slipped because a national summary can hide pockets the virus can still exploit.

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:21.940
Reporting on the outbreak notes that similar events have occurred in other countries when coverage dipped, and that local delivery, who actually receives a visit, decides whether an imported case fades or keeps spreading.

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:39.560
This is being treated as a reach problem as watches a medical one, vials only count if they arrive in the right neighborhoods. In the coming weeks, health agencies will track case numbers and vaccination uptake to see whether those emergency drives are landing in the hardest hit communities.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:50.140
The United Kingdom has imposed sanctions on Israeli settlements in the West Bank. UK officials accused some settlers of carrying out what they described as ethnic cleansing.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:59.440
Israel answered by saying it will shut the UK consulate in East Jerusalem, a move that marks a shift in how London handles settlement-related activity.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:09.840
Settlement expansion has continued for decades, a timeline neither capital disputes, and the fight is over whether penalties from outside can change what happens on the ground.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:31.780
BBC reporting presents the sanctions as a reply to documented settler violence and land seizures that have displaced Palestinian communities. UK officials say the measures aim at individuals and entities directly involved in those actions, and they argue that focused penalties can deter further displacement while still leaving room for negotiated borders.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:38.680
They point to earlier sanctions regimes that isolated extremist elements without stopping all settlement activity.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:47.300
Israeli authorities call the package an unwarranted interference in domestic security matters and a break from earlier diplomatic norms.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:56.100
They frame the consulate closure as a proportionate reply to criticism they see as one-sided and as ignoring wider regional security threats.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:03:08.740
Israeli government statements argue that singling out settlements rewards Palestinian rejection of talks and weekends Israel's ability to manage security and territory it has administered since 1967.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:15.160
They add that previous outside pressure has often hardened positions rather than advancing compromise.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.820
Recurring food safety scandals in China turn on whether inspection can keep pace with how food now moves.

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:31.200
Detection tools and regulatory capacity have grown more sophisticated yet consistent safe production remains hard to lock in the economist reports.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:39.240
Supply chains grew longer and more tangled as the economy expanded and that length has been difficult for oversight to match at scale.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:48.080
Chinese regulators point to new testing technologies as evidence of progress yet enforcement still varies widely from one province to another.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:55.280
The same analysis notes that other large economies needed decades to stabilize after similar industrial transitions.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:04.760
Producers remain under pressure to keep prices low while meeting rising demand and some local officials still put growth targets ahead of strict compliance checks.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:12.260
Cost and speed pull one way, safety checks pull the other and that tension has not disappeared as the tools improved.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:20.540
Estonia currently holds the strongest school system among western countries according to international assessments reported by the economist.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:26.520
Several other wealthy nations have recorded falling student performance over a long stretch of years.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:32.140
Turkish results are cited as a counter trend with gains against that wider slide.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:37.100
British outcomes come through as relatively stable while many peers declined.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:46.680
The reporting attributes Estonia's place to steady spending on teacher training and a coherent curriculum rather than repeated overhauls of the whole structure.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:55.140
Countries that kept a steady focus on classroom conditions instead of frequent system redesigns have been more likely to hold their scores.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:05.040
Deepseek, a Chinese artificial intelligence or AI startup, has hired civic securities to ready a share sale on Shanghai's star market.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:09.500
The firm is trying to raise money at home rather than selling shares abroad.

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:15.680
That path fits a wider push to deepen technology financing inside China, Reuters reports.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:22.620
People backing the company present the listing as a match for national goals of self-reliance in advanced computing.

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:30.580
The process is expected to show how Chinese AI companies are adjusting to a funding climate that looks more inward than before.

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:40.600
A close look at public statements from Elon Musk on AI finds a gap between how fast capabilities are moving and how ready governments are to handle that pace.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:51.600
The economist argues that those predictions, even when they mainly grab attention, expose how few institutions have concrete plans for AI's economic and social effects.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:58.580
Technology policy researchers point to the lack of coordinated standards across major economies as a core weakness.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:05.460
Industry observers add that competition among developers still outruns the regulatory clock in most jurisdictions.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:10.520
What the models can already do is pulling away from the rules meant to guide their use.

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:13.780
There is progress worth knowing in British aviation.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:19.060
Flights from the country's airports have resumed after a major air traffic control failure.

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:27.160
Airports caution that a full return to normal will take more time, because aircraft and crews still have to be moved back into place.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:31.160
The outage had left planes and staff scattered across the network.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:35.720
Operations restarted early on September 9, Reuters reports.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:41.740
Airport operators stressed that safety protocols prevented wider incidents while the system was down.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:49.220
The disruption showed how a single weak point in critical infrastructure can cascade even when backup systems exist.

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:55.480
Recovery work now centers on restoring schedules without creating new bottlenecks at major hubs.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:07:03.080
To really understand why measles keep finding a way back, you have to follow a chain of delivery, trust, and follow-up.

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:05.700
Not a simple shortage of vials in a warehouse.

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:10.340
A lot of coverage treats a shortfall as if the only problem were supply.

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:19.100
The disease needs roughly 95% coverage to stop sustained transmission, because it spread so efficiently through airborne droplets.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:28.140
When routine childhood shots fall below that level in any cluster of communities, an imported case can start chains of infection that last months.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:37.860
Historical records from other countries show that even brief dips during conflict, migration, or strain on health systems can leave whole-age groups unprotected.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:41.600
Those cohorts can then keep an outbreak alive for years.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:48.940
The same dynamic has appeared where mobile populations or remote areas received fewer follow-up visits from health workers.

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:58.660
First dose numbers can look acceptable in a national summary, while second dose completion lags in particular districts, which is how infection chains persist.

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:09.340
When a report cites an overall national rate, check whether district level second dose figures are also moving up, rather than assuming the average capture's localized risk.

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:18.640
A useful check is whether the next official update states the share of affected districts that finish targeted extra vaccination drives within the last 30 days.

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:24.960
Another is whether independent surveillance groups publish separate tallies you can set beside government figures.

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:35.620
Primary records such as district immunization registers remain the clearest picture of where coverage actually stands, and they help separate counted cases from modeled estimates.

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:43.380
If you want to go deeper on health and education system performance, compare how Reuters and the economist are covering those trends.

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:46.520
You will hear two different frames on related facts.

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:55.400
Tomorrow watch for updated vaccination uptake figures from the emergency drives, and for whether more delayed flights return to their published times.

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:57.800
That wraps up today's omniview.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:06.780
